# milky_way_outline.dat
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
#
# The outline of the Milky Way, drawn as a shaded area on the star wheel.
#
# The outline traces the faintest of the five brightness levels in the Milky
# Way Outline Catalog by Jose R. Vieira <http://www.skymap.com/milkyway_cat.htm>,
# as converted into GeoJSON by Olaf Frohn for d3-celestial
# <https://github.com/ofrohn/d3-celestial> (feature "ol1" in data/mw.json).
# Points closer than 0.2 degrees to their predecessor have been dropped.
#
# The band of the Milky Way encircles the whole sky, so its northern and
# southern edges are each a closed ring. The remaining rings outline dark
# regions within the band, such as the Coalsack. The shaded area is everything
# enclosed by an odd number of rings.
#
# Each ring starts with a line containing the word "ring", followed by the
# points along it, one per line:
# 1. Right ascension, J2000, degrees
# 2. Declination, J2000, degrees
#
# The d3-celestial data are distributed under the following licence:
#
# Copyright (c) 2015, Olaf Frohn
# All rights reserved.
#
